## Interface: 100007, 16001
## Title: |cff888888Spoken Zones (now in Spoken)|r
## Notes: Spoken Zones is now part of Spoken, in the Spoken_Zones folder. This folder never loads and is safe to delete.
## Version: 3.3.0
## Group: Spoken
## LoadOnDemand: 1
# A tombstone, with no Lua. Spoken Zones shipped in this folder until 3.0.0-beta.3, which moved
# it to Spoken_Zones: the name SpokenZones belongs to the retired CurseForge project of the same
# name, and the CurseForge app updating or removing a stale install of that project would
# otherwise overwrite or delete the folder Spoken's own download ships the module in.
# scripts/spoken/package-retired.sh writes this file over every .toc name the old folder had on
# Blizzard's clients, each with that client's Interface line (scripts/lib/tombstone.sh), as that
# project's last release. Either way the old copy is left with nothing to load, rather than
# loading beside Spoken_Zones and voicing every line twice. LoadOnDemand keeps the client from
# loading even the empty addon, which is also what keeps Spoken's leftover-folder warning
# (OLD_FOLDERS in addons/Spoken/Core.lua) quiet: it names only a full old copy, which does load.
